config RDMA_RXE
	tristate "Software RDMA over Ethernet (RoCE) driver"
	depends on INET && PCI && INFINIBAND && 64BIT
	depends on INFINIBAND_VIRT_DMA
	depends on RUST
	select NET_UDP_TUNNEL
	select CRC32
	help
	This driver implements the InfiniBand RDMA transport over
	the Linux network stack. It enables a system with a
	standard Ethernet adapter to interoperate with a RoCE
	adapter or with another system running the RXE driver.
	Documentation on InfiniBand and RoCE can be downloaded at
	www.infinibandta.org and www.openfabrics.org. (See also
	siw which is a similar software driver for iWARP.)

	The driver is split into two layers, one interfaces with the
	Linux RDMA stack and implements a kernel or user space
	verbs API. The user space verbs API requires a support
	library named librxe which is loaded by the generic user
	space verbs API, libibverbs. The other layer interfaces
	with the Linux network stack at layer 3.

	RXE requires Rust support, including a supported architecture and
	toolchain. Configurations incompatible with RUST, such as RANDSTRUCT,
	cannot enable this driver. There is no C implementation fallback.

	To configure and work with soft-RoCE driver please use the
	following wiki page under "configure Soft-RoCE (RXE)" section:

	https://github.com/linux-rdma/rdma-core/blob/master/Documentation/rxe.md

config RDMA_RXE_KUNIT_TEST
	bool "KUnit tests for RXE Rust policy" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on RDMA_RXE && KUNIT=y
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Test RXE management datagram encoding, queue resizing, receive queue
	  limits and task scheduling without requiring an RDMA device.
	  They run at boot when RXE is built in, or on loading rdma_rxe when
	  the driver is built as a module.
